WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.631 --> 00:00:07.758
-What's your source?
-What's your source?

2
00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:12.346
My fellow Americans.

3
00:00:12.429 --> 00:00:15.641
as many of you know.
I killed Paul Bunyan today.

4
00:00:15.724 --> 00:00:18.018
I'll take questions in a moment.

5
00:00:18.101 --> 00:00:20.479
Paul James Bunyan was a frontier folk hero

6
00:00:20.562 --> 00:00:22.064
turned modern nightmare.

7
00:00:22.147 --> 00:00:24.608
He used his legendary size
and status to disguise

8
00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:27.694
a 30-year spree of murder.
arson. and cannibalism.

9
00:00:27.778 --> 00:00:29.738
As leader of the nation
that Bunyan helped build

10
00:00:29.821 --> 00:00:31.261
and as the man who took off his head

11
00:00:31.323 --> 00:00:33.242
with an obsidian boomerang.
I'll say this much

12
00:00:33.325 --> 00:00:35.410
to anyone who thinks
they're taller than the law.

13
00:00:35.494 --> 00:00:37.246
Timber. bitch. Questions?

14
00:00:37.329 --> 00:00:38.205
Stuckey.

15
00:00:38.288 --> 00:00:39.891
"The New York Times" recently accused you

16
00:00:39.915 --> 00:00:42.000
of using taxpayer dollars to play Batman.

17
00:00:42.084 --> 00:00:44.127
The "Times" can ask
Paul Bunyan if I was playing.

18
00:00:44.211 --> 00:00:45.045
Munson.

19
00:00:45.128 --> 00:00:46.797
How do you respond to "People" magazine

20
00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.608
calling you the president
with the greatest voice?

21
00:00:48.632 --> 00:00:52.052
I can neither confirm or deny!

22
00:00:52.135 --> 00:00:53.196
Good-looking redhead in front.

23
00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:54.054
Oh.

24
00:00:54.137 --> 00:00:55.532
Uh. do you think killing Paul Bunyan

25
00:00:55.556 --> 00:00:56.974
will hurt your approval rating?

26
00:00:57.057 --> 00:00:59.285
I think the families of the people
he was eating will approve.

27
00:00:59.309 --> 00:01:00.352
Others will disapprove.

28
00:01:00.435 --> 00:01:02.688
like people who print menus
for pancake restaurants.

29
00:01:02.771 --> 00:01:05.566
Look. folks. I took an oath
to protect the people.

30
00:01:05.649 --> 00:01:08.277
And sometimes that means
I won't get likes and subscribes.

31
00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:10.070
If you don't like it. all I can offer

32
00:01:10.153 --> 00:01:12.781
is an emoji of a dinner plate
and an emoji of my ass.

33
00:01:12.864 --> 00:01:15.284
Thank you and God bless America.

34
00:01:15.367 --> 00:01:16.410
Bluebird bound for Oval.

35
00:01:16.493 --> 00:01:17.773
Ma'am. please stay 10 feet back.

36
00:01:17.828 --> 00:01:19.871
Oh. I'm Banks. I'm the new Chief of Staff.

37
00:01:19.955 --> 00:01:20.998
I don't know that.

38
00:01:21.081 --> 00:01:21.957
Oh.

39
00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:23.584
Special Agent O'Doyle.

40
00:01:23.667 --> 00:01:26.295
You run things by the book
when you're not being booked.

41
00:01:26.378 --> 00:01:27.671
Ugh. felon much?

42
00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:29.089
Those charges were dropped.

43
00:01:29.172 --> 00:01:30.817
It's not murder
to finish a ghost's business.

44
00:01:30.841 --> 00:01:33.302
And waving a hologram of me
when I was 3 pounds heavier

45
00:01:33.385 --> 00:01:34.803
does not give you clearance.

46
00:01:34.886 --> 00:01:37.598
I've been cleared to come
into the United States Press Room.

47
00:01:37.681 --> 00:01:40.475
How could I be here
and not be who I say I am?

48
00:01:40.559 --> 00:01:43.162
You could be a dopplegobble.
That's a hybrid of doppelganger and a...

49
00:01:43.186 --> 00:01:44.438
I know what a dopplegobble is.

50
00:01:44.521 --> 00:01:45.439
O'Doyle. what are you doing?

51
00:01:45.522 --> 00:01:46.522
Possible dopplegobble.

52
00:01:46.565 --> 00:01:48.150
There is no possible dopplegobble.

53
00:01:48.233 --> 00:01:49.943
Sir. I'm Chief of Staff Rho Banks.

54
00:01:50.027 --> 00:01:52.321
You might wanna curb Agent Bro
before he shoots me.

55
00:01:52.404 --> 00:01:54.823
Hey! Not in front of press.
All of this is off the record.

56
00:01:54.906 --> 00:01:56.158
That's not how that works.

57
00:01:56.241 --> 00:01:58.428
You have to say something's
off the record before it happens.

58
00:01:58.452 --> 00:02:00.454
What are you. Professor Record?

59
00:02:00.537 --> 00:02:03.832
Steve. why are you checking to see
if your name is Professor Record?

60
00:02:03.915 --> 00:02:06.501
Some kind of creature attacked me
in the Press Bathroom!

61
00:02:09.087 --> 00:02:10.922
Dopplegobble!

62
00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:14.468
Everyone. stay back. Swapping ammo.

63
00:02:14.551 --> 00:02:16.762
Shape-Hold. Shape held.

64
00:02:16.845 --> 00:02:18.472
Swapping again. Mentos.

65
00:02:18.555 --> 00:02:19.765
Cover your mouths.

66
00:02:22.059 --> 00:02:23.894
Well. ma'am. I guess that clears you.

67
00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:24.996
Dopplegobbles are solitary...

68
00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:26.647
I know they're solitary hunters!

69
00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:29.232
OK. put that shit on the record.

70
00:03:00.764 --> 00:03:01.598
OK. OK.

71
00:03:01.682 --> 00:03:03.850
Now unlearn Polish and learn origami.

72
00:03:03.934 --> 00:03:05.811
Oh. and the screenplay for "RoboCop"!

73
00:03:05.894 --> 00:03:07.288
O'Doyle! What... what do you think?

74
00:03:07.312 --> 00:03:09.564
I think she's an unregulated synthetic.

75
00:03:09.648 --> 00:03:11.149
"Well. give the man a hand!"

76
00:03:11.233 --> 00:03:13.443
Origami RoboCop! She can do anything!

77
00:03:13.527 --> 00:03:14.695
Shut yourself down.

78
00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:17.906
Doesn't work like that.

79
00:03:17.989 --> 00:03:19.199
And I'm not a "synthetic."

80
00:03:19.282 --> 00:03:21.910
My brain has just been maximized
for neural plasticity.

81
00:03:21.993 --> 00:03:23.495
Sounds so organic.

82
00:03:23.578 --> 00:03:25.288
Sorry. O'Doyle's half leprechaun.

83
00:03:25.372 --> 00:03:28.166
so he's wary of deception.
magic. et cetera.

84
00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:29.960
Don't leprechauns like those things?

85
00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:32.129
So you've literally hired my mother.

86
00:03:33.338 --> 00:03:34.899
Sir. maybe we should go over
your schedule for today?

87
00:03:34.923 --> 00:03:36.203
You've got that trade meeting...

88
00:03:36.258 --> 00:03:37.578
Hey. you can learn karate. right?

89
00:03:37.634 --> 00:03:38.510
Actually. better question...

90
00:03:38.593 --> 00:03:41.012
if we intercepted one of those
giant Japanese monsters...

91
00:03:41.096 --> 00:03:42.931
-Kaijus.
-If we intercepted a kaiju.

92
00:03:43.014 --> 00:03:45.118
could we put a helmet on it
and have you hack into its brain?

93
00:03:45.142 --> 00:03:46.601
Then we'd have our own kaiju.

94
00:03:46.685 --> 00:03:48.687
That would be a violation
of international law.

95
00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:51.064
Oh. God. you're one of those legal people?

96
00:03:51.148 --> 00:03:52.733
Oh. God. you're not?

97
00:03:52.816 --> 00:03:53.650
Yes. Janice?

98
00:03:53.734 --> 00:03:57.904
Sir. an almost handsome man
from the CIA is here to see you.

99
00:03:57.988 --> 00:04:00.240
Shit. Do not let him provoke you.

100
00:04:00.323 --> 00:04:02.009
Don't mention the names
of anyone you hold dear.

101
00:04:02.033 --> 00:04:03.785
You're afraid of the CIA?

102
00:04:03.869 --> 00:04:05.746
They killed Kennedy. they Nixon'd Nixon.

103
00:04:05.829 --> 00:04:07.748
and I think they stole
one of Carter's fingers.

104
00:04:07.831 --> 00:04:08.871
Don't send him in. Janice.

105
00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:11.084
Nah. nah. send him in.

106
00:04:11.168 --> 00:04:13.420
Hi there. Mr .Presi... gun. gun!
I've got a gun!

107
00:04:13.503 --> 00:04:15.297
Come on. man.
you gotta be faster than that.

108
00:04:15.380 --> 00:04:16.691
Oh. by the way. I'm not from the CIA.

109
00:04:16.715 --> 00:04:18.550
The CIA doesn't exist.

110
00:04:18.633 --> 00:04:19.634
-Or does it?
-Ugh.

111
00:04:19.718 --> 00:04:21.318
Oh. It's this week's new Chief of Staff.

112
00:04:21.344 --> 00:04:22.429
No intro neccessito.

113
00:04:22.512 --> 00:04:23.388
I've read your file.

114
00:04:23.472 --> 00:04:25.265
Targeting Officer Jack Coffey.

115
00:04:25.348 --> 00:04:27.726
Bluff called. She really reads the files!

116
00:04:27.809 --> 00:04:29.019
Loser. So what's your gimmick?

117
00:04:29.102 --> 00:04:30.479
Gotta have an action hero gimmick

118
00:04:30.562 --> 00:04:31.831
or this manchild wouldn't hire you.

119
00:04:31.855 --> 00:04:33.332
Like this guy. You know he never lies?

120
00:04:33.356 --> 00:04:35.150
I'll show you. You gay? He can't answer.

121
00:04:35.233 --> 00:04:36.401
'Cause of the Kinsey scale.

122
00:04:36.485 --> 00:04:37.485
We're all a little...

123
00:04:38.111 --> 00:04:39.279
Except me. I'm lying.

124
00:04:39.362 --> 00:04:41.198
What do you want. you fuckin' sociopath?

125
00:04:41.281 --> 00:04:42.741
Glad you asked.

126
00:04:43.742 --> 00:04:44.868
This. as you know.

127
00:04:44.951 --> 00:04:47.287
is a hockey puck with
a hologram of the country in it.

128
00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:48.955
I thought you might like it.

129
00:04:49.039 --> 00:04:50.919
Plus it came with this cool
telescoping pointer.

130
00:04:51.583 --> 00:04:54.419
Uh-oh. handheld apparatus exceeds
the eighteen-inch limit.

131
00:04:54.503 --> 00:04:56.379
You have been detained by Secret Service.

132
00:04:56.463 --> 00:04:57.672
Please! I don't want to die!

133
00:04:57.756 --> 00:04:59.132
That's my one weakness!

134
00:04:59.216 --> 00:05:01.718
Do you know what it's like
to work for people so deceptive.

135
00:05:01.802 --> 00:05:04.346
they can train you to cry on cue?

136
00:05:04.429 --> 00:05:05.597
Why are you here?

137
00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:07.074
I don't know. we just love presidents.

138
00:05:07.098 --> 00:05:08.391
Bomb. Bomb. Bomb. Bomb. Bomb.

139
00:05:08.475 --> 00:05:09.744
-Bomb. Bomb. Bomb.
-Shit! Move. move. move!

140
00:05:09.768 --> 00:05:10.977
Evacuate West Wing!

141
00:05:11.061 --> 00:05:12.479
Really? First day of work?

142
00:05:12.562 --> 00:05:14.523
Bomb. Fake bomb. sound off.

143
00:05:14.606 --> 00:05:16.149
Fake bomb. vibrate.

144
00:05:16.233 --> 00:05:18.151
Fake bomb. gentle beats.

145
00:05:25.075 --> 00:05:26.660
Yuck. Carter germs.

146
00:05:28.411 --> 00:05:30.914
God damn it!
I can't believe we fell for that!

147
00:05:30.997 --> 00:05:33.250
He went down FDR's fireside shaft!

148
00:05:34.334 --> 00:05:37.170
-O'Doyle. can you scan his aura?
-He went north.

149
00:05:37.254 --> 00:05:39.357
He tends to micromanage.
but he'd probably be a good dad

150
00:05:39.381 --> 00:05:40.858
if he stopped getting in his own way.

151
00:05:40.882 --> 00:05:42.843
OK let's chase him. not humanize him.

152
00:05:42.926 --> 00:05:45.095
-Sir. how do I report this exactly?
-You don't.

153
00:05:45.178 --> 00:05:46.805
But none of this is in the Constitution!

154
00:05:46.888 --> 00:05:48.616
Neither is your mama.
but you did what she told you. right?

155
00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:49.640
Gun.

156
00:05:50.851 --> 00:05:52.394
Revise that. Hologram of a gun.

157
00:05:52.477 --> 00:05:53.520
That wasn't me lying.

158
00:05:53.603 --> 00:05:55.397
-The hologram was a lie.
-We get it.

159
00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:56.565
<i>You. with a gun.</i>

160
00:05:56.648 --> 00:05:58.984
<i>You. not masturbating in a Zoom meeting.</i>

161
00:05:59.067 --> 00:06:01.236
<i>You. proudly attending a school play.</i>

162
00:06:01.319 --> 00:06:04.030
-Could've been a good dad?
-I said probably.

163
00:06:04.114 --> 00:06:05.633
He took something from the tape vault.

164
00:06:05.657 --> 00:06:07.510
he's headed for the exit.
and he fears rejection.

165
00:06:07.534 --> 00:06:09.369
Who craves rejection? Let's go!

166
00:06:14.499 --> 00:06:16.459
Damn it! And he took the fastest one!

167
00:06:16.543 --> 00:06:17.645
Uh. what about one of those?

168
00:06:17.669 --> 00:06:19.629
That's Reagan's experimental vehicle bay.

169
00:06:19.713 --> 00:06:22.024
but it's locked with a facial scanner
that thinks I'm Mr. T.

170
00:06:22.048 --> 00:06:24.134
Fortunately. it's using 1980s encryption.

171
00:06:24.217 --> 00:06:25.886
I should be able to patch in.

172
00:06:25.969 --> 00:06:28.531
-Go left! Right! Go right! Hold. hold!
-No. no! Up. up! Hold. hold!

173
00:06:28.555 --> 00:06:29.556
Very helpful.

174
00:06:29.639 --> 00:06:30.639
Got it.

175
00:06:31.474 --> 00:06:32.350
<i>Come on. Ronald.</i>

176
00:06:32.434 --> 00:06:34.185
<i>Let's go teach gangs how to breakdance.</i>

177
00:06:34.269 --> 00:06:36.163
The car doesn't really talk.
Those are recordings.

178
00:06:36.187 --> 00:06:37.939
<i>There is no such thing as AIDS.</i>

179
00:06:38.023 --> 00:06:39.103
I'm not making it say that.

180
00:06:43.737 --> 00:06:45.030
What are you doing? Ram him.

181
00:06:45.113 --> 00:06:47.365
Ram him? We're in a car.
He's in a wheelchair.

182
00:06:47.449 --> 00:06:49.743
-It's a stolen wheelchair!
-It is still punching down!

183
00:06:56.041 --> 00:06:57.584
OK. now it's punching up.

184
00:06:59.085 --> 00:07:00.295
Ah!

185
00:07:02.964 --> 00:07:04.650
-You get him. I'll get the tape!
-Yes. ma'am.

186
00:07:04.674 --> 00:07:05.717
<i>Impact detected.</i>

187
00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:08.053
<i>Planting evidence to avoid liability.</i>

188
00:07:12.140 --> 00:07:14.184
Are you running at my speed
to make me feel better?

189
00:07:14.267 --> 00:07:15.560
-Did it work?
-Go!

190
00:07:19.564 --> 00:07:20.732
Hey! Bad dog!

191
00:07:21.691 --> 00:07:23.443
Actually. wait. I'm the problem!

192
00:07:23.526 --> 00:07:24.903
All your bad behaviors are because

193
00:07:24.986 --> 00:07:26.696
I'm a lazy. undisciplined owner!

194
00:07:31.910 --> 00:07:32.910
Ah. shit!

195
00:07:40.794 --> 00:07:41.628
He's jigging!

196
00:07:41.711 --> 00:07:43.254
We need to get the hell out of here!

197
00:07:47.884 --> 00:07:49.010
I'm so sorry. sir.

198
00:07:49.094 --> 00:07:50.637
I let you down.

199
00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:52.472
You did not. Breathe.

200
00:07:52.555 --> 00:07:54.641
O Danny boy

201
00:07:54.724 --> 00:07:56.393
The pipes. the pipes are...

202
00:07:56.476 --> 00:07:58.353
Excuse me. Are you the president?

203
00:07:58.436 --> 00:08:00.397
No. I'm a lookalike.
I do mattress commercials.

204
00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:02.649
Oh! You're lucky.
He's a handsome man to look like.

205
00:08:02.732 --> 00:08:03.775
Well. bless your heart.

206
00:08:03.858 --> 00:08:05.503
Got it!
Don't know what it is. but I got it!

207
00:08:05.527 --> 00:08:07.362
-Can we do a selfie?
-You better believe it.

208
00:08:07.445 --> 00:08:09.823
-Um. sir?
-I'm glad you're really not him.

209
00:08:09.906 --> 00:08:11.324
A lot of his policies concern me.

210
00:08:11.408 --> 00:08:12.867
and I don't love that he's divorced.

211
00:08:12.951 --> 00:08:14.577
Yeah. well. stick that up your ass.

212
00:08:14.661 --> 00:08:17.455
Sir. why are there two tapes
of the first Moon landing?

213
00:08:17.539 --> 00:08:19.290
And why is one labeled "real"?

214
00:08:19.374 --> 00:08:21.334
Because they're both real?

215
00:08:21.418 --> 00:08:22.544
Eh. I tried.

216
00:08:23.586 --> 00:08:24.713
This is the Moon landing

217
00:08:24.796 --> 00:08:27.090
the world watched live in 1969.

218
00:08:27.173 --> 00:08:29.426
-and it was all very real.
-Oh. thank Christ.

219
00:08:29.509 --> 00:08:32.220
And this is the Moon landing
that was produced as a backup.

220
00:08:32.303 --> 00:08:33.513
-"Backup"?
-You know. in case

221
00:08:33.596 --> 00:08:35.015
Armstrong landed on the Moon

222
00:08:35.098 --> 00:08:36.575
and said. "God is dead." or even worse.

223
00:08:36.599 --> 00:08:37.684
"God is alive."

224
00:08:37.767 --> 00:08:39.769
<i>-One small step for man...
-Cut!</i>

225
00:08:39.853 --> 00:08:42.022
<i>-The line is "a man."
-That's what I said.</i>

226
00:08:42.105 --> 00:08:43.732
<i>-Then you mumbled it.
-Back to "one."</i>

227
00:08:43.815 --> 00:08:45.734
It was shot during LBJ's administration

228
00:08:45.817 --> 00:08:46.651
by Stanley Kubrick.

229
00:08:46.735 --> 00:08:47.962
<i>Hey. you can't talk to me like that.</i>

230
00:08:47.986 --> 00:08:49.654
<i>Yeah. I can. Think about it.</i>

231
00:08:49.738 --> 00:08:51.114
<i>You're in a fake Moon landing.</i>

232
00:08:51.197 --> 00:08:52.949
<i>You really think
they're gonna let you live?</i>

233
00:08:53.033 --> 00:08:54.409
<i>How you feeling? Frightened?</i>

234
00:08:54.492 --> 00:08:55.492
<i>Struggling to breathe?</i>

235
00:08:55.535 --> 00:08:57.037
<i>Cosmically insignificant?</i>

236
00:08:57.120 --> 00:09:00.248
<i>Good. Now put film in the camera.</i>

237
00:09:00.331 --> 00:09:01.166
<i>-Whoa. so cool.
-Wow.</i>

238
00:09:01.249 --> 00:09:02.393
<i>-Did you see that?
-Amazing.</i>

239
00:09:02.417 --> 00:09:05.170
Unfortunately. it cost twice as much
as the real Moon landing.

240
00:09:05.253 --> 00:09:06.588
and 20 people died making it.

241
00:09:06.671 --> 00:09:08.506
-Jesus.
-Mostly writers. but yeah.

242
00:09:08.590 --> 00:09:10.216
It's good the CIA didn't get this tape.

243
00:09:10.300 --> 00:09:12.093
but they home invaded
the White House today.

244
00:09:12.177 --> 00:09:13.553
We need to expose them.

245
00:09:13.636 --> 00:09:15.555
No. we don't.
because we did something better.

246
00:09:15.638 --> 00:09:16.806
We embarrassed them.

247
00:09:16.890 --> 00:09:18.266
Exposure can be very embarrassing.

248
00:09:18.349 --> 00:09:20.226
This administration doesn't tattle. Banks.

249
00:09:20.310 --> 00:09:22.437
We're adults. We fight ninjas.

250
00:09:22.520 --> 00:09:25.899
Mr. President. the CIA called
